{{/*
The defects that break a claim by answering the WRONG thing.

Both plant a live value where a correct subject produces none, which is
why they need one derived — the sampler the fixture uses, taking its
ALTERNATE member so the planted answer cannot be mistaken for a value
the run legitimately seeded.

A defect that returned the zero here would BE the claim rather than
break it, which is the failure the per-check renderability guard exists
to prevent: where no live value derives, the row ships Argued instead.
*/}}
{{- define "suite.defect.echo-beside-error" -}}
{{ renderExpr (external $.Prove "One") }}({{ printf "%q" .DefectName }},
	func(tb {{ renderExpr (external "testing" "TB") }}) {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Subject) }} {
		return {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Ctor) }}(tb, {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Option) }}(
			func{{ renderParams .AnonParams }} {{ renderReturns .NamedReturns }} {
				// A believable answer beside the refusal. A caller
				// reading the error and one reading the value disagree
				// about what happened, which is the claim's own
				// violation rather than a subject that merely failed.
				{{ .ValueSlot }} = {{ renderSample .Echo }}
				{{ .ErrSlot }} = {{ renderExpr (external "errors" "New") }}({{ printf "%q" .EchoMessage }})
				return
			}))
	}){{ template "suite.frag.defect-reason" . }}
{{- end -}}

{{- /*
The claim a zero would STATE rather than break: the defect has to
produce a live value.

Where the claim names a sentinel this is not the shape — a subject that
owed an error and gave none has already broken it, and the bare return
of answers-anyway says exactly that with no value to derive.
*/ -}}
{{- define "suite.defect.answers-with-value" -}}
{{ renderExpr (external $.Prove "One") }}({{ printf "%q" .DefectName }},
	func(tb {{ renderExpr (external "testing" "TB") }}) {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Subject) }} {
		return {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Ctor) }}(tb, {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Option) }}(
			func{{ renderParams .AnonParams }} {{ renderReturns .NamedReturns }} {
				// A value for a call a correct subject answers nothing for.
				{{ .ValueSlot }} = {{ renderSample .Echo }}
{{- if .FlagSlot }}
				// And the flag that makes it an answer. A caller of this read
				// consults the flag and ignores what came beside it, so a value
				// under a false flag is the miss it was meant to contradict.
				{{ .FlagSlot }} = true
{{- end }}
				return
			}))
	}){{ template "suite.frag.defect-reason" . }}
{{- end -}}

